            <ArticleTitle>[A boy with a painful foot].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A957</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 4-year-old boy visited the emergency department with a painful foot. We diagnosed osteochondrosis of the tarsal navicular, also known as Köhler's disease. The patient was successfully treated with a plaster bandage for 4 weeks.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
